  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">First imports of quinoa from India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;With a DGGF Pre-financing IQF Europe will be able to finance the first shipment of quinoa from India to the Netherlands. The company is currently building its European sales network, and has secured its first customer contract with a buyer in Spain.

Europe is more than 90% dependent on South American quinoa, which leads to high prices, fluctuating quality, and supply chain vulnerability. IQF creates a new trade corridor with India to provide a better, more affordable, and reliable supply.

IQF Europe B.V.(part of the IQF Group) is responsible for importing Indian origin quinoa into the European market. While the local Indian entity focuses on sourcing, quality control, processing coordination, and export preparation, IQF Europe manages the full commercial, contractual, financial, and logistical execution from the Netherlands.

The IQF Group sources quinoa directly from partner farmers in India, carries out quality and residue testing through accredited laboratories, and coordinates outsourced processing and storage at a facility in India. After processing, the product is exported to Europe under IQF Europe&#x2019;s specifications and documentation requirements.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
